From 0ea55f39b583c1e3d113c7834e8e9f237f5cbf7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:03:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: test constitution for the constitution-drain blow fear

borg_danger_physical() adds 150 danger for each monster blow that drains
constitution, plus 100 more when the drain would take the stat below 8,
as the comment 'extra scary to have con drain below 8' says.  The extra
check read the current strength (BI_CSTR) instead of constitution, so a
borg whose constitution was already drained below 8 got no extra fear,
while a borg with low strength but healthy constitution did.

Test BI_CCON, as the strength, dexterity and other drain cases already
test their own stat.  A borg with constitution below 8 now counts these
blows as more dangerous and escapes sooner; a borg with only low
strength no longer overrates them.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#61.
---
 src/borg/borg-danger.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-danger.c b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
index 11efe9f1a..add9a66b6 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-danger.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
@@ -374,7 +374,7 @@ static int borg_danger_physical(int i, bool full_damage)
             /* Add fear for the effect */
             z += 150;
             /* extra scary to have con drain below 8 */
-            if (borg.trait[BI_CSTR] < 8)
+            if (borg.trait[BI_CCON] < 8)
                 z += 100;
             if ((pfe) && !borg_attacking)
                 z /= 2;
-- 
